<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi, I used the GP-02Kit to add GPS to the GD77. <br>I connected the power control to the N/F pin of GP-02Kit. <br>To reduce the consumption, I connected the EN pin of the LP3992 to the N/F pin through a 560 ohm resistor. The total consuption is thus less than 0.6mA (through the MCU "shorted" 10k pull-up).</div></blockquote>I decided to go with the module (not the KIT) because we already have 3v3. To me, the kit is just a module with 5V0 to 3v3 regulator on it. In my opinion, it is a lot cleaner mod using the module.<br><br>I'm not sure about EN on the LP3992 regulator, Is it 5V logic? I don't think you can pull it down the way you are doing it. As I said, it is a lot better to getting rid of the regulator and N/F directly to the module.<br><br>BTW, I don't think the GP-02 support Active Antenna. I might be wrong, but that is how I understand it.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Wed Jun 25, 2025 1:56 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
