		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3365&amp;p=37376#p37376"><![CDATA[
Thank you for all comments,<br><br>After trying with ML1220, ML920, and ML621 backup batteries. I have found out the warm boot on GP-02 will never happened beyond 4 hours. Based on Collins information, I believe this is because the module has to download the ephemeris data due to the expirations of the data it has. From my finding the ML621 is sufficient to back up the module for 4 hours. There is no need for a bigger battery.<br><br>One more thing, the "Battery" on the GP-02Kit is actually NOT a battery. It is a capacitor.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Thu Jun 05, 2025 12:05 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
